course: dictionary
lesson: 3604
title: Fifty: five tens and half
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fifty is the number 50. It is five tens, so count in tens: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50.
explain: Fifty is also half of a hundred. Half of 100 is 50, so fifty is exactly in the middle of 0 and 100. «Fifty years» means fifty of the years, not one.
explain: The words around a number give clues about what it counts. «The red kangaroo can hop at over fifty kilometres an hour.» Fifty is a number of kilometres, and the hour tells you it is a speed.
fact: Fifty is written as 50 and means five tens.
fact: Half of a hundred is fifty.
fact: «Fifty-fifty» means half and half, or an equal chance.
fact: 50 percent is a half, so 50 percent of something means half of it.
fact: In some countries a comma separates euros and cents: «9,50 €» means nine euros fifty.
exercise: «Darya plays the easy bars fifty times.» How many times does she play them? | Five hundred | Twelve | Five | *Fifty
exercise: Which number is half of a hundred? | 500 | *50 | 150 | 25
exercise: «The red kangaroo can hop at over fifty kilometres an hour.» What is fifty measuring here? | Kangaroos | *Kilometres an hour | Tens | Years
test: What does five tens make? | 40 | 15 | 500 | *50
test: What does «fifty-fifty» mean? | Very quick | Fifty people in a line | *Half and half, or an equal chance | Five tens exactly
exam: In the price «9,50 €», what does the 50 mean? | Fifty kilometres | Five euros | *Fifty cents, so the price is nine euros and fifty cents | Fifty euros
